      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are balancing the crushing weight of nihilism with the exhausting fatigue of trying to keep going, which is a very heavy place to be stuck. While logic might suggest letting go if nothing matters, human resilience often thrives not because the void is filled, but simply because holding on offers a small, defined shape to an otherwise infinite emptiness. You are allowed to feel the exhaustion and question the pressure; the goal isn't to fix all of this instantly, but to find a way to exist within that tension without having to force a solid meaning into it. How do you want to navigate the next bit of this feeling?",
      "source": "target",
